      "expected": "The specification states that the 3V3 rail feeds both MCUs, and standard STM32 design requires all VDD pins to be connected to the 3V3 supply and VSS/VSSA pins to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"220\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad100)\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"100\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both MCUs are unpowered and cannot boot, making the flight-control board non-functional.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG3", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["REG3.1", "NAVC2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The LDO output is on net +3.3V, while a separate net +3V3 carries NAVC2 VBAT, connector power pins, and many pull-up resistors but has no connection to the regulator output.",
      "expected": "The design intends one 3V3 rail from the LD39200 LDO to power the MCUs, sensors, connectors, and pull-up networks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") (pintype \"unspecified\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The +3V3 net remains floating/unpowered, so devices and pull-up networks connected to it do not receive 3V3 even if the LDO itself is operating.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC2", "NAVC2", "HSE2", "HSE3"],
      "pins": [
        "FCC2.5",
        "FCC2.37",
        "FCC2.12",
        "FCC2.13",
        "HSE2.1",
        "HSE2.3",
        "NAVC2.5",
        "NAVC2.6",
        "HSE3.1",
        "HSE3.3"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "NET0052",
        "NET0159",
        "Net-(FCC2-PH0)",
        "VREF+_FCC",
        "NET0122",
        "Net-(C102-Pad1)",
        "Net-(NAVC2-PH0)",
        "Net-(NAVC2-PH1)"
      ],
      "observed": "The FCC HSE crystal is connected to PE6/PE7 instead of PH0/PH1, while PH0 and PH1 are connected to decoupling/reference nets. The NAVC HSE crystal is not connected to PH0/PH1 at all; PH0/PH1 have only capacitors, and HSE3 pin 3 leads through R61 to an unconnected net.",
      "expected": "The specification calls for a 25 MHz HSE crystal on the HSE oscillator pins of both STM32 MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"41\") (name \"NET0052\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C22\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"124\") (name \"Net-(FCC2-PH0)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C107\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"PH0\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"83\") (name \"NET0122\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C15\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"HSE3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"142\") (name \"Net-(NAVC2-PH0)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C24\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external high-speed clocks are not applied to the intended MCU oscillator pins, preventing correct clock startup and potentially leaving the MCUs unable to run from the intended 25 MHz HSE source.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows fatal deviations from the intended Hades design: the MCUs are not connected to their 3V3/GND supplies, the 3V3 rail is split into an unpowered +3V3 net and a powered +3.3V net, and the HSE crystals are misconnected/disconnected from the MCU oscillator pins."
}

